ܐܶܓܽܘܪ the form of 1 pers. sing. fut. of three verbs:
a) ܐܶܓܽܘܪ from ↗ ܐܓܪ to hire;
b) ܐܶܓܽܘܪ from ܓܘܪ to commit adultery;
c) ܐܶܓܽܘܪ from ܓܰܪ to drag.
p. 3

ܘܰܨܦܽܘܬܳܐ (?Lê) f. bondage, slavery;
ܢܺܝܪܳܐ ܕܘܰܨܦܽܘܬܳܐ the yoke of bondage
p. 108 108:530,118,909,183

ܘܰܪܩܳܐ or ܘܰܪܩܬܳܐ pl. ܘܰܪ̈ܩܶܐ f. a page, leaf or sheet;
ܘܰܪ̈ܩܶܐ ܕܣܺܐܡܳܐ sheets of silver
p. 108 108:530,1160,909,1221

ܙܗܰܪ fut. ܢܶܙܗܰܪ 1) to be clear, transparent, bright;
ܕܶܒܫܳܐ ܕܙܳܗܰܪ clear honey
2) participial adj. ܙܗܺܝܪ, ܙܗܺܝܪܳܐ, ܙܗܺܝܪܬܳܐ rt. ܙܗܪ. safe, secure, sure, circumspect, prudent, vigilant;
ܣܰܒܪܳܐ ܡܝܰܬܪܳܐ ܙܗܺܝܪܳܐ (?Lê) a most sure hope
with ܠܳܐ imprudent, dangerous, unsafe;
ܡܪܳܕܳܐ ܠܳܐ ܙܗܺܝܪܳܐ (?Lê) an imprudent onslaught
ܐܽܘܪܚܳܐ—ܕܽܘܟܬܳܐ ܠܳܐ ܙܗܺܝܪܬܳܐ an unsafe road, dangerous place
with ܒ careful of, intent upon, watchful over, attentive;
ܙܗܺܝܪܳܐ ܒܢܰܦܫܳܟ watchful over thyself
ܦܓܽܘܕܳܐ ܕܙܗܺܝܪܳܐ ܒܣܽܘܣܝܳܐ the rein which restrains the horse
ܛܰܝܒܽܘܬܳܐ ܕܡܫܺܝܚܳܐ ܙܗܺܝܪܳܐ ܗܘܳܬ ܒܶܗ (?Lê) the grace of Christ kept him safe
with ܕܠܳܐ or ܕܥܒܳܕ (?Lê) taking heed, provident; with ܡܶܢ avoiding, keeping from;
ܒܙܗܺܝܪܽܘ ܟܣܳܝܗ ܡܶܠܬܳܐ ܡܶܢܳܗ (?Lê) he carefully kept the matter from her
ܐܰܝܢܳܐ ܕܙܗܺܝܪ ܡܶܢ ܛܰܢܦ̈ܽܘܬܳܐ whoso keeps far from abominations
Ethpe. ܐܶܙܕܗܰܪ imper. ܐܶܙܕܗܰܪ to take heed, be careful, watch over, guard, keep; to beware, with ܒ of the object cared for, esp. with ܒܢܰܦܫܶܗ of his soul, of himself, with ܡܶܢ of the object to be avoided;
ܐܶܙܕܗܰܪ ܒܶܗ watch over him, guard him
ܐܶܙܕܗܰܪܘ ܕܠܳܐ ܬܶܬܛܰܘܫ ܗܰܝܡܳܢܽܘܬܳܐ (?Lê) take heed lest the faith be defiled
Imper. with ܠ and pers. pron. suff. cave tibi, take care, take warning, take heed to thyself, &c. Pa. ܙܰܗܰܪ to warn, admonish, caution; to take precautions, provide against, make sure, keep safe. Ethpa. ܐܶܙܕܰܗܰܪ to take care, watch over, guard, guard against. Aph. ܐܰܙܗܰܪ a) to shine brightly, flash, lighten;
ܐܽܘܪܚܳܐ ܕܙܰܕܺܝܩ̈ܶܐ ܐܰܝܟ ܢܽܘܗܪܳܐ ܡܰܙܗܪܳܐ the path of the just is as a shining light
metaph.
ܡܰܙܗܰܪ ܒܝܽܘܠܦܳܢܳܐ (?Lê) illustrious
b) to warn, admonish. Derivatives, ܙܗܝܪ, ܙܗܝܪܐܝܬ, ܙܗܝܪܘܬܐ, ܙܗܪܐ, ܙܗܪܝܪܐ, ܙܘܗܪܐ, ܡܙܗܪܢܐ.
p. 111 111:115,961,492,1264;111:504,106,882,668

ܙܳܘܢܳܪܳܐ pl. ̈ܶܐ ζωνάριον, dim. of ܙܳܘܢܳܐ. f. a girdle, belt, worn by monks and priests and Christians generally;
ܥܺܐܕܳܐ ܕܙܳܘܢܳܪܳܐ ܕܡܪܰܬ ܡܰܪܝܰܡ the festival of the girdle of the B. V. M. (West-Syr.)
p. 113 113:506,203,884,316

ܙܽܘܥܙܳܥܳܐ, ܙܽܘܥܙܳܥ rt. ܙܘܥ. m. a violent disturbance, a whirlwind;
ܕܠܳܐ ܙܽܘܥܙܳܥܳܐ unshaken; without disturbance
p. 114 114:136,627,516,713

ܙܽܘܪܳܐ pl. ܙܽܘ̈ܪܶܐ, ܙܽܘܪ̈ܳܬܳܐ rt. ܙܘܪ. m. a handful, the hollow of the hand, palm of the hand, a blow, slap; a measure;
ܟܰܝܶܠܬ ܒܙܽܘܪܳܟ ܥܰܦܪܳܐ ܕܐܰܪܥܳܐ Thou hast measured the dust of the earth in the hollow of Thy hand
p. 114 114:526,282,906,423

ܙܰܛܶܡ or ܙܐܰܛܶܡ denom. verb Pael conj. from ܙܐܛܶܡܰܐ; to investigate, accuse, blame;
ܙܛܶܡܰ̈ܛܰܐ ܕܡܙܰܛܡܺܝܢ ܒܝ the charges they bring against me
Part. ܡܙܰܛܡܳܐ used as adj. culpable, faulty, wrong;
ܡܰܚܫܰܒܬܳܐ ܡܙܰܛܰܡܬܳܐ (?Lê) a wrong opinion
Ethpa. ܐܶܙܕܰܛܰܡ to be blamed, found guilty; to find fault;
ܚܳܣ ܕܢܶܙܕܰܛܰܡ (?Lê) heaven forbid that he be guilty
p. 114 114:526,636,906,845

ܙܺܝܓ Ar. a calendar;
ܙܺܝܓ ܠܡܰܬܠܡ̈ܕܳܢܶܐ (?Lê) a calendar for beginners
p. 114 114:526,1053,906,1114

ܙܺܝܘܳܐ, ܙܺܝܘ pl. ܙܺܝ̈ܘܶܐ m. shining, brightness esp. with ܐܰܦ̈ܶܐ or ܦܰܪܨܽܘܦܳܐ brightness of countenance = cheerfulness;
ܙܺܝܘܶܗ ܫܢܳܐ his looks changed, his countenance fell
p. 114 114:526,1102,906,1209

ܙܳܝܽܘܢܳܐ rt. ܙܘܢ. m. one who feeds, supports, supplies or sustains, a guardian, preserver, sustainer;
ܙܳܝܽܘܢܳܐ ܕܗܽܘܝܽܘ ܡܰܣܝܒܰܪ ܠܟܽܠܳܗ ܒܪܺܝܬܳܐ (?Lê) He is the Preserver who supports the whole creation
p. 115 115:107,109,484,243

ܙܺܝܡܺܝܰܐ pl. ܙܺܝܡܺܝ̈ܰܐܣ f. ζημία, harm, injury, misfortune;
ܙܺܝܡܺܝ̈ܰܐܣ ܣܰܓܺܝܐ̈ܳܬܳܐ ܕܰܗܘܰܝ ܥܰܠ ܟܪ̈ܺܝܣܛܝܳܢܶܐ (?Lê) the many calamities which befel the Christians
p. 115 115:107,442,484,563

ܙܰܝܢܬܳܐ rt. ܙܘܢ. f. a repast, victuals;
ܐܰܫܪܳܐ ܡܳܪܝܳܐ ܙܰܝܢܬܳܟ make lawful, O Lord, the food Thou hast provided
p. 115 115:107,704,484,792

ܙܡܰܪ fut. ܢܶܙܡܰܪ, imper. ܙܡܰܪ, act. part. ܙܳܡܰܪ, ܙܳܡܪܳܐ to sing, chant, play on a stringed instrument;
ܙܡܰܪ ܬܶܫܒܽܘܚܬܳܐ ܠܐܰܠܳܗܳܐ sing praise to God
Ethpe. ܐܶܙܕܡܰܪ to be chanted, sung;
ܩܺܝܬܳܪܳܐ ܕܡܶܙܕܡܰܪ ܒܶܗ harping
ܐܰܝܟ ܕܡܶܙܕܡܰܪ ܠܡܙܰܡܪܳܢܳܐ (?Lê) as was said by the Psalmist
Pael same as Peal; also with regard to David, to say in the Psalms;
ܗܰܘ ܕܡܙܰܡܰܪ the Psalmist = David
Ethpa. ܐܶܙܕܰܡܰܪ to be chanted, sung. Derivatives, ܙܘܡܪܐ, ܙܡܝܪܬܐ, ܙܡܪܐ, ܙܡܪܐ, ܙܡܪܘܬܐ, ܡܙܡܘܪܐ, ܡܙܡܪܢܐ.
